@flexiarg militant-pacifism/remove-causes-not-symptoms
@title Remove the Causes, Not Only the Occurrences
@audience War Machine designers, mission owners
@tone measured
@style pattern
@tier method
@references ["militant-pacifism/demonstrable-harm-reduction" "liberation/mundane/right-effort (prevent and abandon)"]
@status DRAFT 2026-11-05, not approved

! conclusion: When conflict or harm recurs, work on what produces it, and count success by the recurrence stopping, not by each instance being handled.

  + context: War Resisters International: "to strive for the removal of all causes of war." Dhammapada 201: the peaceful live "discarding both victory and defeat" -- the cause is the contest itself, not its outcome.

  + IF:
    Each conflict is resolved as it appears (a lock contention, two agents writing the same file, an operator repeating a correction), so the system gets good at handling conflicts and they keep coming.

  + HOWEVER:
    Causes are slower and less certain to fix than instances, and instance handling is still needed in the meantime.

  + THEN:
    Handle the instance, and record it as an occurrence of a cause. When the same cause recurs, make the cause the work item. Judge it by the recurrence rate afterward.

  + BECAUSE:
    A system that only wins each contest keeps the contests. Removing the cause removes the need for victory and defeat both.
